course: dictionary
lesson: 12939
title: When something keeps annoying you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a thing makes you feel. Exasperating is one of them. It means very annoying, so much that you feel cross and impatient. «The puppy chewed my shoes again and again, which was exasperating.» The word again and again is a clue: the chewing kept happening, and that is what made it so annoying.
explain: Look at the context to find the feeling. In «Alice finds the Caterpillar's short answers exasperating», the answers are short and unhelpful, so Alice feels cross. In «Toad is exasperating to his friends because he never learns», Toad makes the same mistakes over and over, so his friends feel impatient with him.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The bus was late for the third day, which was annoying.» It still makes sense, so annoying is a good match. Exasperating is a little stronger, because the thing keeps happening and wears down your patience.
fact: Exasperating means very annoying, making you feel cross and impatient.
fact: It often describes something that keeps happening, like «the same mistake again and again».
fact: Exasperate is the verb: to exasperate someone is to make them cross and impatient.
fact: Exasperating is an adjective: more exasperating, most exasperating.
fact: Synonyms such as annoying and irritating are close in meaning, but exasperating suggests your patience is being worn down over time.
exercise: «The puppy chewed my shoes again and again, which was exasperating.» What does exasperating mean? | *Very annoying, making you feel cross and impatient | Quiet and calm | Lost and sad | Very tasty and sweet
exercise: Alice finds the Caterpillar's short answers exasperating. What does this suggest? | Quiet enough to make Alice sleepy | Long, kind and very helpful | *Annoying enough to make Alice feel cross | Funny enough to make Alice laugh
exercise: «The rain kept falling all day, and waiting for the bus was exasperating.» What does exasperating tell you about the waiting? | *It was very annoying and frustrating | It was exciting and fun | It was cold and windy | It was short and quick
test: «Toad is exasperating to his friends because he never learns.» Why is Toad exasperating? | Because he always tells the truth | Because he is always asleep | *Because he keeps making the same mistakes and does not change
test: Which sentence uses exasperating correctly? | The cool breeze felt exasperating on the beach. | *Losing my pencil every single day is exasperating. | The birthday cake was exasperating and delicious.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to exasperating? | Tiny | Generous | *Irritating | Peaceful
